{
  "id": "a1-g05",
  "slides": [
    {
      "type": "cover",
      "title": "Plural nouns",
      "subtitle": "Plurales regulares e irregulares",
      "goals": [
        "Formar plurales con **-s**, **-es** e **-ies**.",
        "Memorizar los plurales irregulares más comunes.",
        "Pronunciar bien la terminación del plural."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Plurales regulares",
      "table": {
        "head": ["Regla", "Singular → plural", "Escucha"],
        "rows": [
          ["La mayoría: **+ s**", "book → books, car → cars", "books, cars"],
          ["Termina en -s, -ss, -sh, -ch, -x, -z: **+ es**", "bus → buses, class → classes, watch → watches, box → boxes", "buses, classes, watches, boxes"],
          ["Consonante + y: **y → ies**", "city → cities, baby → babies", "cities, babies"],
          ["Vocal + y: **+ s**", "day → days, boy → boys", "days, boys"],
          ["Muchas en -f / -fe: **→ ves**", "knife → knives, leaf → leaves, wife → wives", "knives, leaves, wives"],
          ["Algunas en -o: **+ es**", "tomato → tomatoes, potato → potatoes", "tomatoes, potatoes"]
        ],
        "speak": 2
      },
      "tip": "Las palabras en -o de origen extranjero o abreviadas solo llevan **-s**: *photos, pianos, videos, radios*."
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Plurales irregulares",
      "table": {
        "head": ["Singular", "Plural", "Escucha"],
        "rows": [
          ["man", "**men**", "man, men"],
          ["woman", "**women**", "woman, women"],
          ["child", "**children**", "child, children"],
          ["person", "**people**", "person, people"],
          ["foot", "**feet**", "foot, feet"],
          ["tooth", "**teeth**", "tooth, teeth"],
          ["mouse", "**mice**", "mouse, mice"],
          ["fish / sheep", "**fish / sheep** (no cambian)", "fish, sheep"]
        ],
        "speak": 2
      },
      "watch": "*Women* se pronuncia /ˈwɪmɪn/, como \"uí-min\". Y *people* ya es plural: **people are**, nunca *peoples are*."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "title": "Plurales en contexto",
      "items": [
        { "en": "There are thirty **students** in my class.", "es": "Hay 30 alumnos en mi grupo." },
        { "en": "I have two **brothers** and three **sisters**.", "es": "Tengo dos hermanos y tres hermanas." },
        { "en": "The **children** are in the park.", "es": "Los niños están en el parque." },
        { "en": "Brush your **teeth**!", "es": "¡Lávate los dientes!" },
        { "en": "These **boxes** are heavy.", "es": "Estas cajas pesan." },
        { "en": "Many **people** live in big **cities**.", "es": "Mucha gente vive en ciudades grandes." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "fill",
      "title": "Escribe el plural",
      "items": [
        { "t": "one bus → two ___", "a": ["buses"] },
        { "t": "one city → two ___", "a": ["cities"] },
        { "t": "one key → two ___", "a": ["keys"], "clue": "Vocal + y: solo **+ s**." },
        { "t": "one child → two ___", "a": ["children"] },
        { "t": "one knife → two ___", "a": ["knives"] },
        { "t": "one woman → two ___", "a": ["women"] },
        { "t": "one watch → two ___", "a": ["watches"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "title": "¿Qué terminación llevan?",
      "buckets": ["+ s", "+ es", "y → ies"],
      "items": [
